::::section {#architecture}
## Architecture {#architecture-heading}

:::figure {#fig-pipeline}
:::image {src="assets/pipeline.svg" alt="NODX parser pipeline from bytes to renderers"}
:::
:::caption
Pipeline from UTF-8 source to canonical AST and renderer-specific output.
:::
:::

:::code {#pipeline-json lang="json"}
{
  "bytes": "UTF-8",
  "parser": "line-oriented",
  "ast": "canonical semantic tree",
  "outputs": ["html", "tui", "ncp"]
}
:::

:::agent-review {#agent-review-block fallback="children" sensitivity="internal"}
The custom component keeps its children readable. A renderer that does not know
`agent-review` can still display this fallback safely.
:::
::::

::::section {#forms-and-records}
## Read-only Records {#records-heading}

:::form {#release-form title="Release readiness"}
:::field {name="parserParity" label="Parser parity" value="pass"}
:::
:::field {name="publicCorpus" label="Public corpus" value="published"}
:::
:::field {name="securityReview" label="Security review" value="pending"}
:::
:::

:::note {#agent-change type="warning"}
Example change record:
:::

:::code {lang="json"}
{"schema":"nodx/change/1.1","op":"set-attribute","target":"#release-form","author":"agent:release-reviewer","reason":"Mark readiness evidence","requiresApproval":true}
:::
::::

::::section {#appendix}
## Appendix {#appendix-heading}

Inline coverage includes [external links](https://example.com), spans such as
[semantic term]{role="term"}, references like @[control-table], variables such
as {{vars.company}}, inline code `nodx ast`, and inline math $$a^2+b^2=c^2$$.

:::pre {#plain-pre}
NODX keeps preformatted text readable.
    Indentation is preserved inside literal blocks.
:::
::::
